[:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/id #uuid "efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{AB}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/id #uuid "87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AF}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/id #uuid "1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/id #uuid "a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/id #uuid "5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{EF}$ and $\\overset{―}{AF}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073740 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/id #uuid "4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-101460" :question/problem "![](images/de/de806ae4a790c7339d49e362204a7a16257a3cb43165e0992f9a35afffed01bd.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons." :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $2$ triangles.\n\nThen, we count the number of hexagons. We see that there are $10$ hexagons.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:10.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,10 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:5$ is equivalent to $2:10.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:5$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $5$ hexagons.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1951351-6ab8-534f-90fd-05b82bf0bde5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1951351-6ab8-534f-90fd-05b82bf0bde5" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1951351-6ab8-534f-90fd-05b82bf0bde5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-81cb9c8e-f7fd-5812-bb11-be5300ffbd38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08513f19-74f5-507e-a4d8-bfb5cd2b45a9" "answer-23d90c48-ea12-53a1-858f-c697d01e819a" "answer-072c4612-620f-5665-ae88-803a5e73fc7c" "answer-81cb9c8e-f7fd-5812-bb11-be5300ffbd38" "answer-31ef6be4-bd24-5a95-b3aa-bc1b412f2eef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08513f19-74f5-507e-a4d8-bfb5cd2b45a9" :answer/id #uuid "08513f19-74f5-507e-a4d8-bfb5cd2b45a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23d90c48-ea12-53a1-858f-c697d01e819a" :answer/id #uuid "23d90c48-ea12-53a1-858f-c697d01e819a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-072c4612-620f-5665-ae88-803a5e73fc7c" :answer/id #uuid "072c4612-620f-5665-ae88-803a5e73fc7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81cb9c8e-f7fd-5812-bb11-be5300ffbd38" :answer/id #uuid "81cb9c8e-f7fd-5812-bb11-be5300ffbd38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31ef6be4-bd24-5a95-b3aa-bc1b412f2eef" :answer/id #uuid "31ef6be4-bd24-5a95-b3aa-bc1b412f2eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064358 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43993959-de6b-5c51-8ec3-a8748bbd2836" "question-89a1fe1c-2eda-5608-9d61-d01a69e48b0c" "question-aa0a4c98-4d7d-54fc-bc9e-2776a355d7bb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-43993959-de6b-5c51-8ec3-a8748bbd2836" :question/id #uuid "43993959-de6b-5c51-8ec3-a8748bbd2836" :question/math-academy-id "q-42849" :question/problem "$240÷(-12)=$" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(240)$ by a negative one $(-12).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n240÷(-12)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $240$ by $12$ without any signs: $240÷12=20.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n240÷(-12)=-20.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e22da01-1a4a-5c86-bce5-b7f59218a6c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e22da01-1a4a-5c86-bce5-b7f59218a6c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e22da01-1a4a-5c86-bce5-b7f59218a6c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c71de70-51c8-5f75-b420-bfb08a683bd3" "answer-15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" "answer-778ca7f1-f188-5a4c-9f4d-93061d1d1614" "answer-e8807038-60fd-56bb-b1ea-3ea4788dbb98" "answer-57aebd5e-28ee-528f-94d6-0490b58ea004"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c71de70-51c8-5f75-b420-bfb08a683bd3" :answer/id #uuid "6c71de70-51c8-5f75-b420-bfb08a683bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" :answer/id #uuid "15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-778ca7f1-f188-5a4c-9f4d-93061d1d1614" :answer/id #uuid "778ca7f1-f188-5a4c-9f4d-93061