field/id #uuid "db184784-f6d4-5c28-8a15-c15b05c79c8f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e" :answer/id #uuid "5b1a8b6b-61be-54ef-8f09-df8cdccda60e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c7d5f96-b21f-5a6d-9152-c11e8ec482aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7d5f96-b21f-5a6d-9152-c11e8ec482aa" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47" :answer/id #uuid "f75deb86-5e5d-5e2d-9cd9-fffa78c81d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578" :question/id #uuid "cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578" :question/math-academy-id "q-269758" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix." :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $2\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 4$ matrix is a $2\\times 4$ matrix." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-10b9c40d-0f99-5165-992c-7ee67c9fdf0b" "answer-field-06a730cb-f6f9-509a-b61c-4cd84171ee45" "answer-field-1632bbd1-d312-5a7f-a64f-22e3b1a7ff52" "answer-field-833c84b1-7ee9-574b-9a22-60778f19bb83" "answer-field-f111d030-ce88-5d03-9b99-a627f5567a44" "answer-field-17626623-6533-5b07-939c-3abf99298482"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-10b9c40d-0f99-5165-992c-7ee67c9fdf0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "10b9c40d-0f99-5165-992c-7ee67c9fdf0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0d226b16-1f62-526c-ace4-04ab4e5f0015" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d226b16-1f62-526c-ace4-04ab4e5f0015"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d226b16-1f62-526c-ace4-04ab4e5f0015" :answer/id #uuid "0d226b16-1f62-526c-ace4-04ab4e5f0015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06a730cb-f6f9-509a-b61c-4cd84171ee45" :answer-field/id #uuid "06a730cb-f6f9-509a-b61c-4cd84171ee45" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6a342a32-6392-5dbb-a213-057659b94404" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a342a32-6392-5dbb-a213-057659b94404"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a342a32-6392-5dbb-a213-057659b94404" :answer/id #uuid "6a342a32-6392-5dbb-a213-057659b94404" :