ix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix." :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $2\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 3$ matrix is a $2\\times 3$ matrix." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06e8af08-6f3d-542f-9c27-ac0092d1e952" "answer-field-3b10feee-49bf-5f48-a752-82ca217efd7c" "answer-field-ce46bf49-6669-5133-a050-5509d649b2d1" "answer-field-6f00946b-80d3-591e-9f55-4d7a50d7a967" "answer-field-37608c1b-6b71-5eee-be39-b1d5820e3583" "answer-field-273ae1bc-6569-51f3-9b52-35e60079ae43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06e8af08-6f3d-542f-9c27-ac0092d1e952" :answer-field/id #uuid "06e8af08-6f3d-542f-9c27-ac0092d1e952" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-829eaf69-efe6-543a-8e00-aaeeb5a7bff9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-829eaf69-efe6-543a-8e00-aaeeb5a7bff9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-829eaf69-efe6-543a-8e00-aaeeb5a7bff9" :answer/id #uuid "829eaf69-efe6-543a-8e00-aaeeb5a7bff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b10feee-49bf-5f48-a752-82ca217efd7c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b10feee-49bf-5f48-a752-82ca217efd7c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-62305239-9216-526d-90d5-03acac93db1c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62305239-9216-526d-90d5-03acac93db1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62305239-9216-526d-90d5-03acac93db1c" :answer/id #uuid "62305239-9216-526d-90d5-03acac93db1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce46bf49-6669-5133-a050-5509d649b2d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce46bf49-6669-5133-a050-5509d649b2d1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-247b61cb-8eb4-5114-8792-a2ebc10cf697" :answer-field/choices ["answer-247b61cb-8eb4-5114-8792-a2ebc10cf697"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-247b61cb-8eb4-5114-8792-a2ebc10cf697" :answer/id #uuid "247b61cb-8eb4-5114-8792-a2ebc10cf697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f00946b-80d3-591e-9f55-4d7a50d7a967" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f00946b-80d3-591e-9f55-4d7a50d7a967" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a551f62f-d8ff-5c79-9764-9e1a62f3bcb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a551f62f-d8ff-5c79-9764-9e1a62f3bcb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a551f62f-d8ff-5c79-9764-9e1a62f3bcb1" :answer/id #uuid "a551f62f-d8ff-5c79-9764-9e1a62f3bcb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37608c1b-6b71-5eee-be39-b1d5820e3583" :answer-field/id #uuid "37608c1b-6b71-5eee-be39-b1d5820e3583" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1401d1ad-903b-53db-9c28-7363827d3400" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1401d1ad-903b-53db-9c28-7363827d3400"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1401d1ad-903b-53db-9c28-7363827d3400" :answer/id #uuid "1401d1ad-903b-53db-9c28-7363827d3400" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-273ae1bc-6569-51f3-9b52-35e60079ae43" :answer-field/id #uuid "273ae1bc-6569-51f3-9b52-35e60079ae43" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-99131c34-2864-51f3-a766-2f1711213fb8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99131c34-2864-51f3-a766-2f1711213fb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99131c34-2864-51f3-a766-2f1711213fb8" :answer/id #uuid "99131c34-2864-51f3-a766-2f1711213fb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dac59390-e4c1-5a03-ac45-73be8ac0d42f" :question/id #uuid "dac59390-e4c1-5a03-ac45-73be8ac0d42f" :question/math-academy-id "q-270271" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1) \\\\ 1-3(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}-3{x}_{1})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3703a9d4-39d0-52e0-b2bc-ee344c22c3a9" "answer-field-488426ab-dda7-531e-996c-ff2ec4f75627" "answer-field-d3e8934b-c392-5107-ac80-32d083b1ab1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3703a9d4-39d0-52e0-b2bc-ee344c22c3a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "3703a9d4-39d0-52e0-b2bc-ee344c22c3a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab" :answer/id #uuid "21a18e2b-10b2-54ed-a6ac-5c17d190f8ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-488426ab-dda7-531e-996c-ff2ec4f75627" :answer-field/id #uuid "488426ab-dda7-531e-996c-ff2ec4f75627" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df" :answer/id #uuid "5292515c-0fe0-52f1-9eb1-46ebf48da0df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3e8934b-c392-5107-ac80-32d083b1ab1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e8934b-c392-5107-ac80-32d083b1ab1b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e" :answer/id #uuid "44580490-2fa0-570f-bccb-1ec9835cc25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78eabbdb-ae14-5218-80c9-de54367d95a9" :question/id #uuid "78eabbdb-ae14-5218-80c9-de54367d95a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-270274" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{3} & 3{y}_{1}^{2}{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot (-1) \\\\ -{1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(-{x}_{1}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(-{x}_{1}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & {x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0c22a089-927d-5420-ba5b-9d5a307d76f3" "answer-field-fa3ff81f-7b33-5955-80fb-a94bca6abd34" "answer-field-e28c09c1-aa3c-5844-9e63-e8909dfcd99f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0c22a089-927d-5420-ba5b-9d5a307d76f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c22a089-927d-5420-ba5b-9d5a307d76f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c" :answer/id #uuid "35d55130-d4fa-5917-b1e0-af08ead2241c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa3ff81f-7b33-5955-80fb-a94bca6abd34" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3ff81f-7b33-5955-80fb-a94bca6abd34" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3" :answer/id #uuid "67ca7192-6580-54d4-9919-f42b30af00f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e28c09c1-aa3c-5844-9e63-e8909dfcd99f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e28c09c1-aa3c-5844-9e63-e8909dfcd99f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751" :answer/id #uuid "3bad7d77-5b3b-5af2-8a59-8f057e347751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5bd6ce37-dfc0-53de-b48f-f0c1cbf86c1e" :question/id #uuid "5bd6ce37-dfc0-53de-b48f-f0c1cbf86c1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-269782" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}(2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}(2{y}_{1}+4{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2}-{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 20 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4bc9ae22-cb20-510a-b7a2-e6f0d1758238" "answer-field-942c7780-6535-5d0f-a664-a1bcb891c110" "answer-field-f2ce961c-2b93-552d-bece-02a4eefb9af4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4bc9ae22-cb20-510a-b7a2-e6f0d1758238" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc9ae22-cb20-510a-b7a2-e6f0d1758238" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60" :answer/id #uuid "d386f327-1b96-53b3-a7e0-f538b69b4b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-942c7780-6535-5d0f-a664-a1bcb891c110" :answer-field/id #uuid "942c7780-6535-5d0f-a664-a1bcb891c110" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab" :answer/id #uuid "23ed8eaa-ca9f-556c-8ad7-26b7d0de8dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2ce961c-2b93-552d-bece-02a4eefb9af4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2ce961c-2b93-552d-bece-02a4eefb9af4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1" :answer/id #uuid "87c362c1-bab8-5afa-ac27-6274d18e5dc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240" :question/id #uuid "316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240" :question/math-academy-id "q-269795" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{2}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & {y}_{1} \\\\ 0 & 2{y}_{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1-1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & {x}_{1} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b37e9bb4-7b51-5e9d-bf67-d5f13bdb4255" "answer-field-14e2587d-142c-5f42-b805-a2dc168df701" "answer-field-288a36d8-5d2d-567a-9ad2-820a7533c15d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b37e9bb4-7b51-5e9d-bf67-d5f13bdb4255" :answer-field/id #uuid "b37e9bb4-7b51-5e9d-bf67-d5f13bdb4255" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675" :answer-field/choices ["answer-208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675" :answer/id #uuid "208e7973-c024-51f5-9e8c-860ada293675" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-14e2587d-142c-5f42-b805-a2dc168df701" :answer-field/id #uuid "14e2587d-142c-5f42-b805-a2dc168df701" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6" :answer/id #uuid "e25c5dab-2ab7-5cc2-9a6f-58bc04896ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-288a36d8-5d2d-567a-9ad2-820a7533c15d" :answer-field/id #uuid "288a36d8-5d2d-567a-9ad2-820a7533c15d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969" :answer-field/choices ["answer-448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969" :answer/id #uuid "448a1728-0e5d-5da5-ad5c-f154b8ecf969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/id #uuid "fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/math-academy-id "q-270269" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{2} & 2{y}_{1} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1) \\\\ 3(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & -24 \\\\ 24 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" "answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" "answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/id #uuid "5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/id #uuid "321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/id #uuid "df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer-field/choices ["answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/id #uuid "709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/id #uuid "a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-269812" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{3},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,-2]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 23 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" "answer-field-763c8765-a9b1-5269-af33-608777d3259f" "answer-field-2bf943b9-df94-524e-bcf5-9dc4bf043905"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/id #uuid "9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-763c8765-a9b1-5269-af33-608777d3259f" :answer-field/id #uuid "763c8765-a9b1-5269-af33-608777d3259f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b" :answer/id #uuid "e950d749-747e-5c10-9923-7ecc4c4e753b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bf943b9-df94-524e-bcf5-9dc4bf043905" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf943b9-df94-524e-bcf5-9dc4bf043905" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f" :answer/id #uuid "5cf884bc-7208-554a-9246-1064a959796f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-622e64f1-e6e7-5b08-85d4-13a13c5f884f" :question/id #uuid "622e64f1-e6e7-5b08-85d4-13a13c5f884f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269804" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{2},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[0,\\,0]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -15 \\\\ 16 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-100411ea-c301-524c-9670-31f318b91b8d" "answer-field-c6666e26-39f4-552b-a7aa-0c5ac20b05b6" "answer-field-d50b99a6-09a2-5bf8-a1ca-65bc1edb698c" "answer-field-b25dc009-09b5-5ac7-9218-9efff302f392"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-100411ea-c301-524c-9670-31f318b91b8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "100411ea-c301-524c-9670-31f318b91b8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537" :answer/id #uuid "49ec15b7-9a76-5f20-9b36-a1b00add3537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6666e26-39f4-552b-a7aa-0c5ac20b05b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6666e26-39f4-552b-a7aa-0c5ac20b05b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-accc3c42-57e9-5709-b528-8e32d